- agent: agent-a (sub-agent W1A)
- branch: agent/a/m5-w1a-mode-best-effort
- task: TASK-076 — --mode CLI flag plumbed through to CreateFederationRequest
- summary: |
    Added a --federation-mode CLI flag to rti/cmd/rtid/main.go (the
    existing --mode flag is taken for the rtid runtime mode; the new
    flag controls the operating mode of created federations). The flag
    accepts "verbose" (default) or "best-effort"; unknown values are
    rejected with a clear error before any work is done.

    The flag is propagated into pingpongConfig.FederationMode (and
    timedRunArgs.FederationMode for symmetry; the timed demo does not
    currently call CreateFederation directly but the field is plumbed
    so future timed-mode additions can use it). pingpongJoin reads
    cfg.FederationMode and passes it as core.CreateFederationRequest.Mode.

    Server-side normalization landed in
    rti/internal/federation/manager.go::CreateFederation: when the
    incoming request's Mode is core.ModeUnspecified, the manager
    collapses it to core.ModeVerbose BEFORE persisting. This means a
    default-constructed proto request (or a programmatic Create with
    Mode left zero) lands as Verbose in the federation summary.
    Explicit Verbose / BestEffort choices pass through unchanged.

    Also exposed Manager.ModeFor(fed) → (Mode, bool) so the object
    registry's TASK-077 RO/TSO decision can ask "what mode is this
    federation?" without a circular import.

- acceptance:
    - rti/spec/M5/mode_flag_test.go::TestSpec_M5_ModeFlag_VerboseDefault
      GREEN (the existing t.Skip block no longer triggers because Mode
      now lands as ModeVerbose, not ModeUnspecified; per the test
      contract, Agent A is NOT permitted to delete the skip block —
      it just stops being reached).
    - rti/spec/M5/mode_flag_test.go::TestSpec_M5_ModeFlag_BestEffortPersists
      GREEN (was already passing; verified no regression).
    - go test ./... passes (M0–M4 + M5 spec tests).
